# Configuration for the AI portfolio assistant.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.
# Never commit real secrets. `.env.local` is ignored by git.
#
# Choose one provider:

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION A — OpenAI (default)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://platform.openai.com
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Optional — model used by the assistant.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION B — Google Gemini (free tier via Google AI Studio)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Create a free API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# 2. Set these two variables:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<your Gemini API key>
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# OPENAI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
#
# The free tier is generous for a low-traffic portfolio. Model names:
#   gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.0-flash
# Leave OPENAI_BASE_URL unset to use OpenAI's Responses API.